From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sapphire <sapphire@local>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0400: Display pipeline fixes - stride/geometry, cache coherency, VSync, early console

This patch consolidates fixes for the SpringBoard frame generation/display pipeline:

1. Stride/Geometry/Scaling Fixes:
   - Correct sweetfb_scale handling (2x vs 3x for 1080x2400 panel presented as 1125x2436)
   - Fix rowbytes calculation for BGRA8888 (4 bytes/pixel, 64-byte alignment)
   - Fix logical-to-physical coordinate mapping in present() and swap()
   - Fix SweetHID touch coordinate scaling to match display presentation

2. TTBR0/Physmap/Cache Coherency:
   - Add dc cvac / dsb sy after CPU blitting to panel memory
   - Add dc civac / dsb sy before GPU reads from surfaces
   - Fix write-combine memory handling for MDP scanout buffers

3. VSync/Throttled Present/Deadlocks:
   - Fix mach_absolute_time to nanoseconds conversion for 60Hz grid
   - Fix lock inversion between fLock and fPresentLock
   - Fix missed VSync when GPU copy takes longer than 16.67ms
   - Increase flipWhenCopied timeout from 20ms to 33ms (2 frames)

4. Early Console Contention:
   - Fix debug console vs IOMFB/SpringBoard handoff
   - Ensure console pauses before first frame copy
   - Add boot-arg sweetfb_console_hold to delay console pause

5. SweetSurface plane rowbytes fix (from 0318):
   - Add bytesPerRow at +0x10 in lock result for IOSurfaceGetBytesPerRowOfPlane

6. Low DDR pool fix (from 0233):
   - Ensure SweetLowBuf uses write-combine cache for MDP scanout

7. Pipeline improvements (from 0334):
   - Fix flip ring race conditions
   - Add proper memory barriers for flip_head/flip_tail

